  "presentation_summary": [
    "A 27-year-old intravenous/subcutaneous heroin user presented with 12 hours of generalized muscular stiffness, intermittent sweats, and progressive difficulty opening her mouth.",
    "Examination showed risus sardonicus, trismus with less than 5 degrees of mouth opening, paroxysms of severe sweating while afebrile, and multiple involuntary tonic spasms of neck retraction and trunk extension without loss of consciousness.",
    "She had multiple skin abscesses consistent with infected injection sites.",
    "The clinical diagnosis of severe tetanus was later supported by a low tetanus antitoxin titre and growth of mixed Clostridia species from injection-site abscesses.",
    "In ICU she developed increasing spasms, respiratory arrest requiring intubation and paralysis, and marked autonomic instability with BP swings from 80/40 to 230/130 mmHg and sinus tachycardia 120-150 bpm."
  ],
